00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.750
You're the one that suggested doing the promo.

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:56.650
Ah, here we go.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.740
You guys...

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:02.160
You guys probably wanted to make an excuse and have me do everything, right?

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:11.070
Hey, why did you decide to attend high school?

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:13.760
The truth is-

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:15.380
Don't talk as if you understand me!

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.320
Let me borrow this.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:21.180
Bye.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.930
Ah, about the promo,

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.440
we're working on finishing it on our own right now.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.840
It's amazing!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.240
We're making things turn in 3D and 4D!

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.940
If you don't believe me, come take a look during the General Assembly for yourself.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:34.940
Bye!

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.700
4D... what an idiot!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.310
I'm just checking.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:47.580
That's all I'm doing.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.400
There's no way they can do it.

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:57.980
Embarrass yourselves at the General Assembly.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.300
That's what you guys deserve!

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.780
This polygon didn't disappear.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.050
Ah, you're right.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.160
They really continued to work on it...

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:21.820
...4D?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.910
Ah, Mu-chi!

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.650
Where'd you go?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.490
Dinner?

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.410
I had to do something.

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:31.590
This is none of my business.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.560
I fell asleep.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.820
They're probably not there anymore.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.850
No one would be there at a time like this-

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.050
I'm so sleepy...

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.080
Mu-chi, come on!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.490
Let's get some coffee.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.130
Let's take a little break.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.390
Agreed.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.560
Me, too.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.670
Okay, black coffee then?

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.060
Give me a very strong one.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.580
Get me one, too.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:08.230
Why...

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:10.490
Why are they...

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.810
Why are they going so far to do this?!

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.830
Hey, about Mei...

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:20.590
I understand that you want to complete the 3D stuff Mei created,

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:23.150
but why are you so concerned with Mei?

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:25.210
Because you want her in the Student Council?

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:28.100
No, it's not like that.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:33.750
I don't really talk to Mei-chan that much, so I'm not sure.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:34.950
But I always ask...

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.960
...why is Mei-chan attending school?

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.210
Mei-chan is good at everything she does.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:45.480
Nowadays, there are many ways for people to make a living even if they drop out of school.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:51.340
So, I think Mei-chan is attending school in search of something.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.560
Something, as in?

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.110
I don't know.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.800
But, it's not just studying.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.190
I mean, she came to help us.

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:03.940
When no one else was interested in the Student Council,

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.800
Mei-chan helped out.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.740
I... I...

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.060
I want to become her friend.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:14.970
I want to become friends with Mei-chan.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.550
I want to eat lunch with her,

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.010
to study with her,

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.390
to have fun with her,

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.880
to have worries together,

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.590
to spend time together.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:27.450
I want to spend these precious three years with Mei-chan!

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:28.700
Then...

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.660
Then someday I can ask her.

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.950
"Have you found what you were looking for?"

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:38.200
I want to be able to hear her answer...

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.000
...by becoming Mei-chan's friend.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.880
What do you think?

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.480
That's fine; it's just like you.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.450
Yeah.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.510
Thanks.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.050
Well, let's get working again.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.500
I...

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:05.980
I...

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:07.360
I...

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:08.820
I w...

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:15.730
I wa...

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.790
I want to-

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:46.870
I have found what I've been looking for.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.680
No, I'd found it already.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.180
What's the matter?

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.460
No, nothing.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.820
White pig...

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.450
No, not that...

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.750
It's fish cake...

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.740
Maybe three people will come...

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.410
Oh no!!

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.600
W-We fell asleep!

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:24.870
M-Mikan-chan!

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:25.930
Mu-chi!

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:28.270
What are we going to do?!

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:32.220
What is this?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:34.910
This is...

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.450
That girl...

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.490
It's the little people!

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.960
It must be the little people!

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.710
The little people came out while we were sleeping-

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:48.300
Sure.
The little people came out while we were sleeping-

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.530
For this year's School Fair,

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.550
instead of telling you what you should do,

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.960
we want to give you the freedom to do this or to do that...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.270
...and let you decide on your own plans.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.900
Mei-chan didn't come after all.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.610
I guess it'd be awkward for her.

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:10.180
So, to begin, we at the Student Council,

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:13.880
made a promotion video to ask you
"what do you think of this kind of School Fair?"

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:14.610
Please have a look.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:30.920
Those girls made this?

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:32.710
Apparently.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.560
What's wrong?!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.010
I-I don't know.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.810
Huh? Huh?

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.270
It's no good.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:53.150
Why did it freeze?

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:54.380
Is it...

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.200
Is it my fault?

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.110
Hey, should we temporarily postpone the Assembly?

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:01.740
No!

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:03.750
I will not...

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.030
I will not give up!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.440
We'll probably... have to postpone.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:10.720
Yeah...

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.080
I won't give up.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.710
Because... Because...

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.250
Manabi-chan...

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.720
Mei-chan!

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.980
Re-login to the image cluster.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.240
Disconnect the node that caused the panic.

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:40.410
Determine the unneeded
process ID and send a kill signal.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:48.210
Re-mount temporary and execute directory.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:52.000
execucampus_festapromo.cry

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.140
Enter!

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:09.600
Wow...

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:46.550
Hey, Momo.

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:51.190
I won't be asking you "where in the world were you?" when we had a lot of trouble.

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:52.600
But, what are they doing?

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:54.920
A victory pose, apparently.

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:02.160
How stupid.

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:03.750
Gosh.

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:11.810
But, you actually made all that CG in one night?

00:23:11.810 --> 00:23:13.370
I was late, though.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:14.090
Huh?

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:16.220
It wasn't the little people?

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:17.800
Ow.

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:23.280
And thus, the General Assembly ended successfully.

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:26.810
And there was one more bit of good news...
